  "question": {
    "text": "The first and second ionisation enthalpies of a metal are <math><mn>496</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4560</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, respectively. How many moles of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> respectively, will be needed to react completely with <math><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of the metal hydroxide?",
